/*
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Ottilie contract test — inputs on the PRIVATE Azure Blob (az://), for Azure Batch / Seqera
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Same 2-sample / 4-chromosome test as `ottilie_test`, with every input an az:// path on
    the private `aletest` container. This is the profile a Seqera Launchpad entry should name.

    Usage:  tw launch <entry> -p docker,ottilie_test_az   (outdir supplied per run)
            nextflow run main.nf -profile ottilie_test_az,docker -c conf/azure_batch.config

    ⚠️ `outdir` is deliberately NOT set here. publishDir overwrites but never deletes, so a
    reused directory silently accumulates stale outputs from older pipeline versions and makes
    any comparison untrustworthy. Supply a fresh dated one per run — that is the single value
    the Launchpad's parameters box should still carry.

    WHY az:// AND NOT THE PUBLIC https PROFILE (`ottilie_test_ci`):
      - Inputs stay intra-region and private instead of crossing the public internet each run.
      - The pre-built reference files, the snpEff cache directory among them, sit next to the
        GenBank on this container, so an older launch on those files still resolves. (A directory
        cannot be staged from an https URL; az:// stages it natively.)

    ⚠️ THE WORK DIR MUST BE IN THE SAME CONTAINER (`aletest`) as these inputs whenever the run
    uses the Entra service principal: Nextflow mints ONE container-scoped SAS and reuses it for
    every blob URL, so a node cannot read another container even in the same storage account.
    See docs/dev-practices/azure_batch_execution.md §3.

    ⚠️ A LAUNCHPAD RUN CLONES FROM GITHUB, NOT FROM YOUR WORKING TREE. Edits to this file do not
    reach a Platform launch until they are committed AND pushed to the registered revision.

    Data layout, and how this 2-sample set differs from the 4-sample pilot:
    docs/benchmarking/ottilie_xenobiotic_ale/blob_layout.md
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
*/

// Container + versioned prefix. Override for a v2 prefix or a different account.
def az_base = System.getenv('OTTILIE_AZ_BASE') ?: 'az://aletest/ottilie/v1'

// Callers and joint-germline settings are shared with every other ottilie profile.
includeConfig 'ottilie_common.config'

params {
    // No config_profile_name/description on purpose (2026-09-01): the Launchpad entry serves
    // ad-hoc runs on other datasets too (a user overrides `input` in the form), and profile-set
    // strings would label every such run "Ottilie test" in the banner and MultiQC. The entry
    // name (yAMP-ottilie-test-az) still identifies genuine test runs; ottilie_pilot_az keeps
    // its strings — pilot runs are always what they say they are.

    // Input — samplesheet whose fastq_1/fastq_2 are az:// paths
    input                      = "${az_base}/samplesheet_test_az.csv"

    // Output — TIMESTAMPED, so two launches can never publish into the same directory.
    // publishDir overwrites but never deletes, so a reused outdir silently mixes two runs'
    // outputs; that already produced one uncitable artifact (seqera-runs/2026-08-07-01).
    // A dated literal in a params file relies on someone remembering to bump it — this does not.
    // Override for a specific destination by setting `outdir` at launch (params-file beats config).
    // ⚠️ Evaluated when the head node parses the config, so a `-resume` publishes to a NEW
    //    directory rather than the original run's. Pass an explicit outdir when resuming.
    // ⚠️ Read the run's actual outdir from the Nextflow banner or the Platform run detail — it is
    //    not visible in the launch form, because Platform never evaluates a profile.
    outdir                     = "az://aletest/seqera-runs/yAMP-out-test-${new java.util.Date().format('yyyyMMdd-HHmmss')}"

    // Reference: ONE GenBank, the 4-chromosome SUBSET (_test), not the full genome. The run builds
    // the FASTA, the snpEff database (named S288C_R64_test after the file) and the report's gene
    // track from it. The pre-built files stay next to it on the blob for older launches.
    // ⚠️ The Launchpad entry's parameters box must change in the same step as this file reaches
    //    the registered revision: a box that still carries fasta / snpeff_cache / report_gff3
    //    next to this `genbank` stops at start-up (one reference route only).
    genbank                    = "${az_base}/S288C_reference_test/S288C_R64_test.gb"

    // Mutation report — the igv-reports dashboard. ON.
    // Pinned rather than inherited: it matches the nextflow.config default today, but a Platform
    // run should not silently change behaviour if that default ever moves. (Deliberately NOT in
    // ottilie_common.config — the local profiles leave it inherited, and the nf-test drives it
    // through its own `when` block.)
    generate_reports           = true

    // The workspace these az:// runs are launched from: makes the Seqera run id in the mutation
    // report index a link (<this>/watch/<run id>). A run cannot learn it — set it per deployment.
    seqera_workspace_url       = 'https://cloud.seqera.io/orgs/DTU-Biosustain/workspaces/RECON-ALE'
}
